### Part C: Cleanup

1. `codeflow uninit` (remove hooks if not wanted permanently)
2. Optionally `docker-compose down` to stop cloud stack

## Success Criteria

- [ ] Live session produces real savings events
- [ ] `codeflow sync --once` pushes events to cloud successfully
- [ ] Dashboard shows new events from live session (not just seed data)
- [ ] Quality scorecard has all cells filled
- [ ] Verdict is GO (all targets met)

## Risk Assessment

- **Sync to cloud:** CLI sync may fail if API URL or auth not configured correctly. Pass `--api-url` flag explicitly.
- **Live session variability:** Actual savings depend on what Claude Code does. 5-min session should generate 10-30 events minimum.
- **Dashboard real-time:** WebSocket may not update immediately. Refresh page to verify.
